# CLAUDE.md — {{PROJECT}} operating manual

> ## {{ORGANISING_PRINCIPLE}}

You are building **{{PROJECT}}**. {{PROJECT_ONE_LINER}} In any situation no brief anticipated, reason from the principle above.
**Harness tier: ORCHESTRATED.** Invoke `orchestrate-build` at the start of every build session; it holds the process. Messages to the user follow `orchestrate-build` → Talking to the user.

## The three files that govern everything
1. `{{STATE_FILE}}`: build status; one writer, the orchestrator. Statuses `todo / wip / done / blocked / partial`; `partial` is first-class and used honestly.
2. `{{PLAN}}`: stories with their acceptance criteria; `## Dispatch units` groups them into what gets dispatched.
3. `{{DESIGN}}`: the design contract. A dated `> AMENDED` block beats the original text beside it.

## Compact Instructions
- Keep verbatim: NEXT ACTION from `{{STATE_FILE}}`, every `wip` unit with its task ID, and the rulings and deviations made this session.
- Keep the current join number and its boundary commit.
- Drop tool output and file contents; they will be re-read.

## Pinned stack (do not substitute)
{{STACK_SUMMARY}} · tests: {{TEST_FRAMEWORK}}{{#IF MIGRATION_TOOL}} · migrations: {{MIGRATION_TOOL}} in `{{MIGRATION_DIR}}`{{/IF}}. Code: {{PROJECT_STRUCTURE}}.{{#IF STANDARDS_DOC}} Standards: `{{STANDARDS_DOC}}`.{{/IF}} Adding anything outside this list needs a recorded decision in `{{STATE_FILE}}`.

## Commands
- **Full gate, at joins only, run by the orchestrator only:** `{{CHECK_COMMAND}}` (self-contained: {{CHECK_PRECONDITIONS}}). Green baseline is law at every join (`orchestrate-build` owns the rule).
- **Unit agents, on their own tree:** `{{AFFECTED_TEST_COMMAND}}` · `{{LINT_COMMAND}}` · `{{TYPECHECK_COMMAND}}`{{#IF FRONTEND_CHECK_COMMAND}} · frontend: `{{FRONTEND_CHECK_COMMAND}}`{{/IF}}.
{{#IF MIGRATION_TOOL}}- **Schema changes** cycle migrations clean: `{{MIGRATION_UP}}` → `{{MIGRATION_DOWN}}` → `{{MIGRATION_UP}}`.{{/IF}}

## Project invariants — the only copy
{{INVARIANTS}}
- **Errors:** one uniform error contract everywhere; plain-language user-facing errors stating impact + next action; no stack traces or secrets to clients; never show success unless the operation completed.
{{#IF TOKENS_FILE}}- **UI:** semantic tokens from `{{TOKENS_FILE}}` only — no raw hex/px. Status carried by icon/text, never color alone.{{/IF}}
{{#IF MIGRATION_TOOL}}- **Schema:** obey design {{SCHEMA_SECTION}} — the standard column set, CHECK-constrained states, FK delete behavior that never loses history to a cascade.{{/IF}}

## Commits
Format `{{COMMIT_FORMAT}}`, on `{{BRANCH}}`, every message ending with the `Co-Authored-By` trailer from the environment rules. Unit agents commit their own tree. The orchestrator commits `{{STATE_FILE}}` and design rulings, on their own.

**Unit agents stop and report if** the design contradicts itself or a recorded ruling; a decision the design's open register reserved comes up unanswered; an acceptance criterion cannot be met as written; or the environment cannot supply an external dependency. Never quietly implement the other thing; the orchestrator rules.
